        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nThis was already discussed in #321. The resolution was that [it is not (easily) possible under current design](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/321#issuecomment-1612540171). The alternatives are:\r\n- Use [`go` and `gO`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/04f8d6e0acd5a52d01ec1c392e3947135dbfd8ef/doc/mini-basics.txt#L234-L235) from 'mini.basics'.\r\n- Use [custom mappings](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/321#issuecomment-1539603757).\r\n- Use `['\\r'] = { output = { left = '\\n', right = '\\n' } }` as custom surrounding, but that would not work for indented lines.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
